It was founded by [[Abe no Seimei]] and influenced by [[Onmyodo]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Encyclopedia of Shinto詳細 |url=https://d-museum.kokugakuin.ac.jp/eos/detail/?id=9907 |access-date=2023-03-06 |website=國學院大學デジタルミュージアム |language=ja}}</ref> It is highly linked to the [[Abe clan]].<ref name=":0" />  

Tsuchimikado Shintō was abolished in [[1870]] with the ban of [[Onmyōdō]], and only permitted again in 1945 with religious freedom and the abolition of [[State Shinto]].<ref name=":0" /> 

