{{Ill|Tensha Shinto|lt=Tensha Shinto|ja|天社土御門神道}} is a form of {{Interlanguage link|Confucian Shinto|ja|儒家神道}}. It is related to [[Tsuchimikado Shinto]] <!-- Should it be the same thing? I'm not really sure about the difference -->

It was founded by [[Abe no Seimei]] and influenced by [[Onmyodo]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Encyclopedia of Shinto詳細 |url=https://d-museum.kokugakuin.ac.jp/eos/detail/?id=9907 |access-date=2023-03-06 |website=國學院大學デジタルミュージアム |language=ja}}</ref> in the 1700s<ref>{{Cite book |last=Cali |first=Joseph |url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=J1gEEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA137&lpg=PA137&dq=tsuchimikado+shinto&source=bl&ots=YfpQ3j7eJw&sig=ACfU3U0Vw_cEjeeagB39pGmGf9odGMQnrQ&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwic0ZfnvMj9AhVmAzQIHSidCxUQ6AF6BAgzEAM#v=onepage&q=tsuchimikado%20shinto&f=false |title=Shinto Shrines: A Guide to the Sacred Sites of Japan’s Ancient Religion |last2=Dougill |first2=John |date=2012-11-30 |publisher=University of Hawaii Press |isbn=978-0-8248-3775-4 |language=en}}</ref> It is highly linked to the [[Abe clan]].<ref name=":0" />  

Tsuchimikado Shintō was abolished in [[1870]] with the ban of [[Onmyōdō]], and only permitted again in [[1945]] with religious freedom and the abolition of [[State Shinto]].<ref name=":0" /> A new organization was created for it in [[1953]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=shinbutsu-shugo |title=Shinto and Buddhism |url=https://shinbutsu-shugo.tumblr.com/post/623571458201927680/onmy%C5%8Dd%C5%8D-is-an-initiatory-practice-and-someone-who |access-date=2023-03-06 |website=Tumblr}}</ref> 

